    "narrative": "LawDog\u2019s lineup for June 13th is anchored by **Taylor Ward** (71.19) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (67.16), both of whom benefit significantly from a favorable matchup against Randy V\u00e1squez. **Taylor Ward** represents our strongest play due to his high-leadoff placement, which guarantees maximum plate appearance potential, paired with a massive 19-point efficiency boost from V\u00e1squez\u2019s high xERA. Similarly, **Jeremiah Jackson** and **Gavin Sheets** (64.98) are positioned to exploit the weak pitching environment, with both receiving an identical 19-point SP skill bump. While **Gleyber Torres** (66.30) faces a tougher matchup against Joey Cantillo, his impressive 13% platoon efficiency boost makes him a high-floor start at MI, providing necessary stability while we navigate a slate where several key arms are hovering near the 3.00 xERA mark.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Jung Hoo Lee** (48.90), who barely missed the cut. While he offers a unique advantage against Ben Brown with a 100% SB delivery boost, his score ultimately fell below our efficiency threshold compared to the high-upside profiles of **Gavin Sheets** and **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.73). We are also exercising caution with **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez** (57.86); despite being a cornerstone of our offense, the matchup against an elite Tarik Skubal (2.82 xERA) coupled with a penalty for Skubal\u2019s ability to limit SBs keeps his score in the mid-range. With **Jonathan Aranda** (62.38) and the rest of the squad relying on assumed lineups, we are monitoring potential late-scratch risks, particularly given the volatility of the weather patterns impacting the park factors for our outfielders. We are proceeding with this lineup to maximize daily efficiency while maintaining strict discipline on our remaining game caps.",
